# Each upstream revision is recorded once and restated in agreement.
#
# A revision cannot be stated only once: a Cargo manifest reads no file,
# a captured fixture carries what it was captured against, and a
# third-party notice has to name what it notices. So the pin file is
# where the revision is decided, and every restatement is held to it —
# in both directions. A site that stops carrying the pin has dropped out
# of the set the pin governs; a site carrying a revision no pin file
# records is the drift a pin exists to prevent.
#
# The count is pinned too. Without it a site could be dropped from the
# list and the check would pass over a smaller world, which is the way
# a gate like this usually stops meaning anything.

# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/upstream-pins.py %S/../.. | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: 12 pin statements agree
